# Test Strategy

## Philosophy
Shift-left: Tests written before or with implementation. Production-like environments. Fail fast, fail safe.

## Test Pyramid

| Layer | Percentage | Purpose | Tools |
|-------|-----------|---------|-------|
| Unit | 70% | Isolate logic, fast feedback | Jest/Vitest/Pytest |
| Integration | 20% | Component interaction, API contracts | Supertest/MSW |
| E2E | 10% | Critical user flows, cross-system | Playwright/Cypress |
| Contract | 100% coverage | API consumer/provider agreement | Pact |
| Performance | Key paths | Latency, throughput, stability | k6/Artillery |
| Chaos | Resilience | Failure injection, recovery | Gremlin/Chaos Monkey |

## Coverage Requirements

### Mandatory 100% Coverage
- Authentication/authorization flows
- Payment/financial transactions
- Data persistence operations
- API contract implementations

### Minimum 90% Coverage
- Business logic services
- Utility functions
- Error handling paths

### Minimum 80% Coverage
- Configuration and setup
- Logging and observability

### Exempt (with documentation)
- Framework boilerplate
- Generated code

## Critical Flows (Must Never Break)

| ID | Flow | Test Type | Frequency |
|----|------|-----------|-----------|
| CF-001 | User registration → onboarding | E2E | Every PR |
| CF-002 | Authentication → session management | Integration | Every PR |
| CF-003 | Core transaction (payment/data) | E2E + Contract | Every PR |
| CF-004 | Data export/deletion (GDPR) | E2E | Daily |
| CF-005 | Error recovery → graceful degradation | Chaos | Weekly |

## Test Data Strategy

- Unit tests: Factory pattern, randomized valid data
- Integration tests: Test containers, isolated databases
- E2E tests: Staging environment, seeded data, cleanup
- Never use production data in tests

## CI/CD Integration

- Pre-commit: Lint, type check, unit tests (< 2 min)
- PR: Full unit + integration + contract tests (< 10 min)
- Merge: E2E critical flows + security scan (< 20 min)
- Nightly: Full E2E + performance + chaos (< 60 min)

